1
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:07,423
TWO MONTHS EARLIER

2
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,350
They say that in this world,

3
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:20,020
no one stays your friend
or your enemy forever.

4
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:24,732
Which means that anyone
can stab you in the back at any moment

5
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:26,401
for their own personal gain.

6
00:00:27,069 --> 00:00:29,154
There's no telling
when you might be betrayed.

7
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,951
But here's the saying
that rings truer to me right now.

8
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:38,079
"The enemy of your enemy is your friend."

9
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:43,459
-  Sir!
- Sit down, sit down, it's okay.

10
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,127
At ease, guys. At ease. Sit down.

11
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,296
Colonel Ahn.

12
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,799
Sorry I'm late.

13
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,884
It's fine. Haven't been here long.

14
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:54,720
Can you believe it's so hot
at this time of night?

15
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:55,973
Tell me about it.

16
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:59,517
I appreciate you showing up, Colonel.

17
00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:02,270
If you call me, Geonyoung,
then I come running.

18
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:04,397
- Excuse me?
- Yeah?

19
00:01:04,398 --> 00:01:06,482
Two bowls of gukbap
and one order of suyuk please.

20
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:07,484
You got it.

21
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:09,902
- You're drinking, right?
- Yeah, sure.

22
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:11,904
- Here.
- Oh, uh…

23
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,739
It's hot out,
I'm gonna get a beer instead.

24
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,908
All right.

25
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,539
-  Can I grab a beer?
-  Sure.

26
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:24,585
Here, you want some?

27
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:28,212
I always tried to see you
at the prosecutor's office,

28
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,214
but you avoided me.

29
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:34,176
Yeah, that's why I wound up
an unemployed loser,

30
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:36,679
and you turned into a bigwig
of national security.

31
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,808
Oh, come on now.
You know, ever since high school,

32
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:43,561
I've just been trying to catch up to you,
and I'm still way behind.

33
00:01:53,864 --> 00:01:55,073
Ah, that's nice.

34
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:57,492
When I heard about you,

35
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,995
I was wondering how you were doing
and what you might be up to.

36
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:03,582
You should've reached out sooner.

37
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:06,543
You think I wouldn't be able
to help you out?

38
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:09,713
So what have you been doing all this time?

39
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:12,256
I mean, what options did I really have?

40
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:14,800
You know
those Gangnam apartments?

41
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,303
- I worked on all those.
- You worked construction?

42
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,306
Not a lot of options
for an ex-con.

43
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:23,852
Sometimes you take crappy jobs
to put food on the table.

44
00:02:27,356 --> 00:02:29,441
Well, thanks.

45
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:37,032
Ah, that's good.

46
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,368
Mmm.

47
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:41,995
Oh.

48
00:02:45,374 --> 00:02:46,583
Your hand…

49
00:02:47,918 --> 00:02:51,629
Yeah, I hurt it a little.
I, uh, can't straighten it anymore.

50
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:53,881
Oh, wow.

51
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:56,093
Guess I'm an invalid now.

52
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,144
What's in the bag?

53
00:03:07,145 --> 00:03:10,941
Well, I had to have
something to show after all these years.

54
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:12,526
Take a look.

55
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:22,118
BAEK KITAE
CHEON SEOKJUNG

56
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,161
Chief Cheon Seokjung.

57
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,789
His slush fund records.

58
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,958
It's 70 billion won.

59
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:35,841
Seventy billion?

60
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,094
BAEKHO TRADING CEO BAEK SOYEONG

61
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:44,432
You and your agency can't
just serve as lackeys

62
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,143
for the KCIA forever, right?

63
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,604
You should take advantage
of your opportunities.

64
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,400
Oh, we're their lackeys?

65
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:57,737
When did you

66
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:01,073
have time to do all of this?

67
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,325
It wasn't that long.

68
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,870
Just took seven years.

69
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:49,915
Now,

70
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,417
I want you to swear you'll do one thing.

71
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:54,668
Tell me what it is.

72
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:57,631
Once you take down Cheon Seokjung
and Baek Kitae, promise me

73
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:00,300
you'll help me get my old job back.

74
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:05,347
I can't live as an ex-con
for the rest of my life.

75
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:08,390
Can I?

76
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,392
I'm shocked

77
00:05:10,769 --> 00:05:13,188
by how much you've changed.

78
00:06:13,582 --> 00:06:15,249
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

79
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:27,094
Ah, I'm glad you're here, Colonel Baek.

80
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,889
Good afternoon, sir.

81
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,058
- You been waiting long?
-  He just got here.

82
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:36,062
Well, take a seat.

83
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,109
Baek, go ahead.

84
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:42,861
Take a seat.

85
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,366
All right, let's see,
do I have everything?

86
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,207
Oh, thanks.

87
00:06:59,002 --> 00:07:02,672
Two soldiers…  …ought
to share a few smokes, am I right?

88
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:04,257
Huh?

89
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:06,468
Here. Oh.

90
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:10,305
- Mmm.
- What are you doing? Don't be rude.

91
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,777
Well, Colonel Baek,
I'm excited to work with you.

92
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,946
Starting tomorrow,
you'll be reporting here.

93
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:30,909
Help him. Give him the support he needs.

94
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:36,372
We should go grab lunch together.
After all, we're a team now.

95
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:37,374
Sounds good.

96
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:41,503
Mmm. Excuse me.

97
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:49,510
This is Jang Geonyoung.

98
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:09,906
IKEDA YUJI …70 BILLION THROUGH
BAEKHO TRADING FROM 1974 TO 1979

99
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:14,869
Baek, I'm sorry,

100
00:08:15,829 --> 00:08:19,249
but we'll have to have lunch
some other day.

101
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,585
I've got to head out.

102
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:26,673
Make sure
he doesn't call anyone.

103
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:33,096
Well, Colonel, we'll see you tomorrow.

104
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:37,809
Uh, by all means,
take your time and finish your cigarette.

105
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:41,438
-  All right. See you later, sir.
- Mm-hmm.

106
00:09:21,186 --> 00:09:22,479
Open fire!

107
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,516
Mr. Baek Kitae.

108
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:08,817
Long time no see.

109
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:11,528
What the…

110
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:15,031
I'm a special advisor to the JIH.

111
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:20,410
Ikeda Yuji.

112
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,080
Or should I say, Choi Yuji.

113
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,125
You two haven't changed at all.

114
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,544
What the hell are you up to? What is this?

115
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:31,297
What's it look like? I'm doing my job.

116
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,051
Get her out of the car.

117
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,387
Get your hands off her. Hey!

118
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:41,307
What do you think you're doing?

119
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,018
You assholes don't know who I am, huh?

120
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:46,019
We're on orders from General Hwang.

121
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:49,148
He received a tip
concerning national security.

122
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:50,900
Please cooperate, Director Baek.

123
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:52,901
What tip, soldier?

124
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:56,280
That a member of the Yakuza
is smuggling 70 billion won in cash

125
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:57,448
into the country.

126
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:02,453
And now the acting KCIA director just
happens to be riding in a car with her.

127
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:04,289
So then…

128
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:07,792
how about me and you
have a chat later in private?

129
00:11:09,544 --> 00:11:10,587
Listen to me.

130
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:13,840
You're going to go wait quietly
at the KCIA.

131
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:17,885
Unless you want bigger problems with me.

132
00:11:17,886 --> 00:11:19,095
What…

133
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:23,016
you gonna shoot the director?

134
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,779
Let's go.
There's no reason to pick a fight.

135
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,949
- We'll talk at the station.
- Take her away!

136
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,242
Get the money.

137
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,660
Son of a bitch.

138
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,206
Damn it!

139
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:43,553
They took Choi Yuji to the
Joint Investigation Headquarters, and--

140
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:44,639
What about the money?

141
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,350
They took all of it.

142
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:56,233
DEPUTY DIRECTOR PYO HAKSU

143
00:12:56,234 --> 00:12:57,527
What a shit show.

144
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,992
Those fucking bastards.

145
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:06,369
At least it's not me.

146
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:14,918
They can talk all they want
about constitutional reform

147
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,838
and direct presidential elections,

148
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:21,258
but in the end, the only thing
that changes the world is money.

149
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:27,639
Bitches!

150
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,433
Politics is no different
than business.

151
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:33,645
Trust, confidence,
loyalty, even people…

152
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:37,274
at the end of the day, all of these things
can be bought with money.

153
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:42,238
The money
I intercepted from Baek Kitae

154
00:13:42,864 --> 00:13:46,284
was supposed to secure the presidency
for Cheon Seokjung.

155
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:50,288
But now, I'm going to take it

156
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,497
and use it as a weapon.

157
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:54,416
It's finally time

158
00:13:54,417 --> 00:13:56,377
to go for my enemies' throats.

159
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,767
Wow.

160
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:13,478
Seventy billion.

161
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:16,980
Baek lined his pockets, huh?

162
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,065
If it weren't for you,

163
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:21,193
it looks like he would've
sucked the whole country dry eventually.

164
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:24,947
I wonder what exactly

165
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:27,449
his plan was here, you know?

166
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:31,245
Cheon Seokjung had
to have some larger end goal.

167
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:34,582
I mean, how would you even spend this?

168
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:37,627
Baek Kitae wants to swallow
this country whole.

169
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:40,713
In one go.

170
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:44,341
That sneaky, thieving little bastard.

171
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:47,761
We have targets now.
Baekho Trading is first.

172
00:14:47,762 --> 00:14:49,889
And then Cheon Seokjung's slush fund

173
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,891
will be tied to Baek's meth operation.

174
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,852
Which means that we can
destroy them for good.

175
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:56,938
Uh…

176
00:14:58,064 --> 00:15:01,192
that's going to be… pretty difficult.

177
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:06,988
We haven't had a memorial service
for the president yet.

178
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:07,990
Hang on.

179
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:12,161
What does that have to do
with taking down Baek?

180
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:16,081
Bringing him down is fine,
but it's the meth…

181
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:18,501
It's gonna look bad.

182
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:21,838
Uh, I'm confused.
What do you mean by that?

183
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:24,422
We're after him because he's dealing meth.

184
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:29,512
Ah, somehow you're still not getting it.

185
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:33,473
Jang, look. Think about this for a second.

186
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:36,894
If it gets out that the men closest
to the president were pushing drugs,

187
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:40,022
how do you think
the public's going to respond?

188
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:44,025
Essentially, it would end up
with the president's name

189
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,277
being dragged through the mud.

190
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:49,656
We have to preserve the legacy
of this country's leadership, don't we?

191
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:52,451
He's a drug pusher
and he'll pay the price. Simple as that.

192
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,331
General Hwang.

193
00:15:58,708 --> 00:16:00,333
We have an opportunity

194
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:03,336
to make it clear to the public
how we deal with criminals.

195
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:06,716
This is how we root them out
and get rid of drug pushers for good.

196
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:10,093
This is how we preserve
our country's legacy and protect--

197
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:12,221
All right,
I understand what you're saying.

198
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:17,310
Let's just circle back to this after
the president's official memorial service.

199
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:21,396
For now, leave the meth out of it
and bring him down with the money.

200
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:24,150
Look, we have plenty of it
right in front of us, don't we?

201
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,444
That'll keep things…

202
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:30,072
…nice and squeaky clean.

203
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:38,956
You all right?

204
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,792
What happened to Choi? Did you find out?

205
00:16:42,293 --> 00:16:43,878
Mmm, well…

206
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:48,007
they took her to the JIH
to interrogate her.

207
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:50,092
Can you believe that?

208
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:53,304
Jang Geonyoung teamed up with those guys.

209
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,641
Never thought I'd live to see that.

210
00:16:57,225 --> 00:16:58,309
And the money?

211
00:16:59,393 --> 00:17:01,812
I assume
they'll be holding onto it for a while.

212
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,734
All done.

213
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,031
The good news is…

214
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,369
they still don't have
any hard evidence yet.

215
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:20,289
They can't do much
with that kind of money right away.

216
00:17:20,915 --> 00:17:22,625
As long as Choi doesn't start blabbing.

217
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,005
How do you think
Jang Geonyoung knew where to go?

218
00:17:30,925 --> 00:17:32,343
There's gotta be a leak.

219
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:35,263
From Japan, or someone who works with us.

220
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:45,481
So, do you think Choi can hold out?

221
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:49,151
They'll probably put her through hell.

222
00:17:55,116 --> 00:17:56,659
Get out.

223
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:03,082
Hey.

224
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:05,459
I expect you to greet me, asshole.

225
00:18:08,379 --> 00:18:09,463
Just say…

226
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:11,215
Piece of shit.

227
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:32,737
I did a thorough sweep, sir.

228
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,988
There were no bugs.

229
00:18:34,989 --> 00:18:36,949
There's nothing to be concerned about.

230
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,952
Put a few guys on Pyo Haksu.

231
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:45,790
I want a report on everything,
everyone he meets.

232
00:18:45,791 --> 00:18:47,335
Of course, sir. I'm on it.

233
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:52,130
Takahashi Kazuo.

234
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:54,799
He's stuck by Choi Yuji's side
for ten years.

235
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,802
My guess is, he's been holding onto
the ledger for a while.

236
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:58,887
PERSONAL RECORD

237
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:00,930
Knowing Yuji,
there's no way she'd keep the money

238
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,558
and the ledger in the same place.

239
00:19:03,351 --> 00:19:05,978
If that ledger gets found
by anybody in the JIH,

240
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,564
we'll be dead. So go find him now.

241
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,399
Copy that.

242
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:44,850
- A yakuza from Osaka named Choi Yuji.
- Yeah?

243
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:00,449
Section Chief Park.

244
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:05,204
Yeah? I got it.

245
00:20:06,497 --> 00:20:07,665
How have you been, sir?

246
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:10,667
Oh. Baek, what are you doing here?

247
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:13,294
I received an assignment here
that begins this morning.

248
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,921
- I'm looking forward to--
-  Oh, no.

249
00:20:14,922 --> 00:20:17,049
Come on, you didn't have to do this.

250
00:20:17,842 --> 00:20:19,135
All right, thanks.

251
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,386
You have any questions, let me know.

252
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:22,972
Thanks, sir. Much appreciated.

253
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:25,558
Oh, Baek.

254
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:27,393
Yes, sir?

255
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:30,812
Did you hear about it?

256
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:32,022
Hear about what?

257
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:34,315
Ikeda Yuji, we caught her.

258
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,110
Word is she's a member of the Yakuza.

259
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:37,902
Why was she brought in?

260
00:20:37,903 --> 00:20:41,239
She brought money into Busan illegally.
And lots of it.

261
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,658
How much?

262
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:48,789
Seventy billion.

263
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:53,042
Just imagine how many cartons
70 billion would buy you.

264
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:57,339
Anyway, thanks for these.

265
00:20:57,923 --> 00:20:59,508
Sure.

266
00:21:16,609 --> 00:21:18,694
Oh, good morning, ma'am.

267
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:22,822
Miss Oh, a Yakuza woman named Choi Yuji

268
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:25,116
got busted for smuggling 70 billion won.

269
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:26,201
Seventy billion?

270
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:28,162
Yeah, it's making waves in the department.

271
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:55,397
Choi Yuji. You brought her in here?

272
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,066
Yes.

273
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:00,318
Hey, you

274
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:03,072
could've told me about this beforehand.

275
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,367
Why exactly would I do that?

276
00:22:06,951 --> 00:22:08,285
What good would that do?

277
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:12,414
Well, never mind.

278
00:22:18,921 --> 00:22:21,924
The raw materials for their meth
came in from Taiwan.

279
00:22:23,801 --> 00:22:25,718
So I'm gonna get a warrant

280
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:28,222
for Baek Soyeong, now that we have proof.

281
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:34,603
You wanna give it a shot?

282
00:22:35,563 --> 00:22:37,106
Take a crack at Choi Yuji?

283
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:38,649
Really?

284
00:22:40,651 --> 00:22:41,652
Mmm.

285
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:45,906
Miss Choi Yuji.

286
00:22:46,949 --> 00:22:49,742
Why did you smuggle
70 billion won into Korea?

287
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,789
Did Baek Kitae put you up to it?

288
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:04,300
All of that money
came from selling meth, isn't that right?

289
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:08,721
And then you went and laundered it
into Chief Cheon's slush fund.

290
00:23:12,308 --> 00:23:15,060
Hey, Miss Choi.
What, can't you talk?

291
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:22,442
You're just gonna keep your mouth shut?

292
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:25,779
You clearly don't understand
the situation you're in.

293
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:29,198
Yeah, you probably think
the whole world just turns for you

294
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,326
with a face like that.

295
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:33,871
You got another thing coming.

296
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,791
Yeah, and how would you know?

297
00:23:38,292 --> 00:23:39,293
Moron.

298
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,420
What?

299
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:44,131
"Moron?" Hey.

300
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,636
Listen to me carefully.

301
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:53,723
Right now, Korea's under martial law.

302
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:56,392
So the military controls
the whole country.

303
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:57,894
Got it?

304
00:23:57,895 --> 00:24:00,147
You know what that means
for your situation?

305
00:24:01,315 --> 00:24:02,316
What's your point?

306
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:04,360
You think I care?

307
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:06,694
You know I'm Japanese, right?

308
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:11,825
That makes no fucking difference!
Doesn't mean a damn thing!

309
00:24:12,534 --> 00:24:15,620
Are you listening?
I said Korea is under martial law.

310
00:24:15,621 --> 00:24:18,998
Which means
everything is different right now.

311
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:21,752
And nobody in this country
is playing by the rules anymore.

312
00:24:22,878 --> 00:24:26,130
It doesn't matter where you're from,
'cause you're not in Japan!

313
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:27,840
You're in Korea!

314
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:31,427
If you're not careful,
a little yakuza girl like you

315
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:33,137
could wind up dead in no time.

316
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:35,557
Is that funny?

317
00:24:38,185 --> 00:24:40,479
Yeah. All right, I get it.

318
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:46,902
- Just give me a smoke, okay?
- What?

319
00:24:48,404 --> 00:24:50,030
You little bitch.

320
00:25:35,492 --> 00:25:39,496
I bet you think you and Baek Kitae

321
00:25:41,081 --> 00:25:42,708
are gonna last forever.

322
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:47,671
You've shared a bed…

323
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,758
…you've shared your money…

324
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:55,596
You two have shared everything. Right?

325
00:25:56,221 --> 00:26:00,517
I mean, a pair of drug pushers
in love with each other?

326
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:04,187
That's pretty crazy. Right?

327
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:05,938
Not very romantic, is it?

328
00:26:09,777 --> 00:26:12,362
Hey, am I wrong about you two?

329
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:15,157
So the ledger

330
00:26:17,076 --> 00:26:19,286
for Cheon's 70 billion won fund.

331
00:26:20,162 --> 00:26:21,830
If you can get it for me,

332
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:25,250
you'll walk out of here alive.

333
00:26:26,001 --> 00:26:27,086
Hmm?

334
00:26:32,216 --> 00:26:34,426
I have Japanese papers, sir.

335
00:26:35,302 --> 00:26:37,554
Contact the embassy, they'll sort it out.

336
00:26:38,806 --> 00:26:41,182
The prosecutor told you
nobody cares about that.

337
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:42,434
Were you not listening?

338
00:26:43,393 --> 00:26:44,894
Don't give me that crap.

339
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:47,981
The country's under martial law.
You know you're screwed.

340
00:26:49,691 --> 00:26:52,027
Tell me where I can find it. The ledger.

341
00:26:55,531 --> 00:26:57,658
I have Japanese papers, sir.

342
00:26:59,201 --> 00:27:01,078
Please contact the embassy.

343
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:06,959
Listen, smart-ass.

344
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:11,296
Do you hear that?

345
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:16,926
Really, can you hear that? Are you deaf?

346
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:23,976
You're a criminal.

347
00:27:28,564 --> 00:27:30,106
Okay, tough guy.

348
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:31,275
Now you listen to me.

349
00:27:32,276 --> 00:27:33,527
You have two choices.

350
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:37,865
You either die and vanish in here,
or you walk out alive.

351
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,785
Where's the slush fund ledger?

352
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:13,942
Get in here!

353
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:17,946
Tie her up.

354
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:40,677
You staying, Prosecutor Oh?

355
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:44,264
You can leave if you don't wanna watch.

356
00:28:57,945 --> 00:28:59,111
Choi Yuji.

357
00:28:59,112 --> 00:29:02,323
The ledger for Cheon's slush fund,
tell me where it is.

358
00:29:02,324 --> 00:29:03,492
Right now.

359
00:29:16,630 --> 00:29:19,800
Kitae, I have a feeling
the KCIA is crawling with rats.

360
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:22,719
Isn't it?

361
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:30,227
How the hell did they know where to go?

362
00:29:32,813 --> 00:29:33,814
Sir, it's my fault.

363
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:39,903
Now what?

364
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:44,866
We're just gonna let someone else
walk away with all of it?

365
00:29:45,701 --> 00:29:48,953
Without the money, that shit heel
Hwang Daesik is gonna string us up

366
00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:50,663
from the nearest tree as soon as he can.

367
00:29:50,664 --> 00:29:52,707
I'll put everything back in order.

368
00:29:52,708 --> 00:29:54,083
Just give me more time.

369
00:29:54,084 --> 00:29:55,836
Are fucking kidding me?

370
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:05,971
I hear your brother joined
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

371
00:30:12,144 --> 00:30:13,270
What, you…

372
00:30:14,521 --> 00:30:15,856
you weren't aware?

373
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:21,193
You don't talk
to your own brother anymore?

374
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:25,782
Can you really…

375
00:30:27,868 --> 00:30:29,285
trust him after this?

376
00:30:29,286 --> 00:30:32,038
My brother is not going to be a problem.

377
00:30:32,039 --> 00:30:35,375
When it comes down to it,
and you're fighting for money and power…

378
00:30:38,587 --> 00:30:40,255
…sharing blood is meaningless.

379
00:30:43,717 --> 00:30:45,926
BAEKHO TRADING
ORGANIZATION CHART

380
00:30:56,188 --> 00:30:58,314
- Chief.
- What is it?

381
00:30:58,315 --> 00:31:02,152
This guy here,
he's a junior from my neighborhood.

382
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:06,323
So what was Hwang's response?

383
00:31:08,492 --> 00:31:10,159
He can't be persuaded.

384
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:12,579
He's the most stubborn bastard
I've ever met.

385
00:31:13,246 --> 00:31:15,582
And we haven't

386
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,751
even had a service for the president yet.

387
00:31:18,752 --> 00:31:21,213
Slow down. Let's pull back a little.

388
00:31:23,215 --> 00:31:24,508
Look, sir.

389
00:31:25,759 --> 00:31:28,762
We're military men. Soldiers.

390
00:31:29,304 --> 00:31:31,348
Our job is to obey orders.

391
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:34,726
You've been around the block.
You should know that by now.

392
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:36,394
Well,

393
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:39,730
I should probably get back to work.

394
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:54,620
Uh-huh, I'm on it. Yes.

395
00:31:54,621 --> 00:31:56,288
I'll make sure I look into it. All right.

396
00:31:56,289 --> 00:31:58,208
You can't
write the story like that.

397
00:31:59,668 --> 00:32:02,504
Hey, Miss Oh, um,
you wanna grab a drink? I wanted to--

398
00:32:11,555 --> 00:32:13,056
70 BILLION THROUGH BAEKHO
TRADING FROM 1974 TO 1979

399
00:32:19,521 --> 00:32:20,647
Come in.

400
00:32:22,149 --> 00:32:23,942
Excuse me, sir, do you have a minute?

401
00:32:26,153 --> 00:32:27,445
What is it?

402
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:35,536
You settling in, Baek? Feel at home?

403
00:32:35,537 --> 00:32:37,205
Yes, sir. It's been fine.

404
00:32:44,546 --> 00:32:45,881
Baek Soyeong.

405
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,800
I'll get a warrant to bring her in.

406
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:52,387
Hold off for now.

407
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:54,639
Why?

408
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:57,225
Hold off.

409
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:58,977
Why should I?

410
00:33:00,854 --> 00:33:02,688
Are you being difficult right now?

411
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,149
Can you just try to explain your approach?

412
00:33:05,150 --> 00:33:07,359
Why am I supposed to stand down?

413
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:09,404
Because you take orders from me!

414
00:33:10,155 --> 00:33:11,531
You are not…

415
00:33:16,036 --> 00:33:18,746
You are not doing anything
without my approval.

416
00:33:18,747 --> 00:33:19,831
But why?

417
00:33:21,416 --> 00:33:23,877
Don't tell me the higher-ups
are stopping you again.

418
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:30,926
Just focus on the slush fund for now.

419
00:33:31,468 --> 00:33:33,802
Our first priority is finding the ledger,

420
00:33:33,803 --> 00:33:35,096
then we go for Cheon,

421
00:33:35,597 --> 00:33:36,973
and finally, Baek Kitae.

422
00:33:42,646 --> 00:33:44,522
All right, let me ask you something.

423
00:33:46,066 --> 00:33:47,984
Are you sure going this far is…

424
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:49,945
responsible?

425
00:33:54,366 --> 00:33:55,491
Say more.

426
00:33:55,492 --> 00:33:57,535
Look, going after Baek is one thing.

427
00:33:58,078 --> 00:34:00,038
Torturing prisoners is something else.

428
00:34:01,498 --> 00:34:03,291
I know times have changed and everything.

429
00:34:04,793 --> 00:34:06,628
But everyone deserves dignity.

430
00:34:07,379 --> 00:34:09,297
People deserve basic human rights.

431
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:13,635
You saying I should feel guilty
for the way I handle a bunch of animals?

432
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:19,683
Is that it?
You want to go back to the old days?

433
00:34:22,435 --> 00:34:24,354
Tell me what you want from me.

434
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,066
How is it that becoming a prosecutor
didn't change you one bit?

435
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:32,779
The country is being turned upside down.

436
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:37,492
Yeah, what about you?

437
00:34:39,035 --> 00:34:40,870
Because you've obviously changed.

438
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:46,334
Get out.

439
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:50,004
Go on.

440
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:17,365
BAEKHO TRADING INC.

441
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:29,502
What the hell? Shit.

442
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:31,421
I guess they're closed.

443
00:35:36,343 --> 00:35:37,761
Hey, where'd you say she lived?

444
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:40,054
Remember,

445
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:43,140
we're getting meat delivered today,
so marinate some bulgogi.

446
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:46,478
And either throw the abalone out
or take it home. It's not fresh.

447
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:49,188
Oh, and get the snacks ready
for Minju on time for once.

448
00:35:49,189 --> 00:35:50,565
Yes, ma'am.

449
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:53,693
Wow.

450
00:35:54,736 --> 00:35:55,862
Is that hanbok new?

451
00:35:57,739 --> 00:35:59,365
It's been a long time, Miss Baek.

452
00:35:59,366 --> 00:36:00,784
How's your daughter been?

453
00:36:05,330 --> 00:36:07,289
PROSECUTOR OH YEJIN

454
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:10,627
A prosecutor?

455
00:36:12,754 --> 00:36:14,005
Well, look who's moving up.

456
00:36:14,673 --> 00:36:15,799
I know, right?

457
00:36:17,050 --> 00:36:19,010
I even get to eat pineapple now.

458
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:21,262
Mmm. That's tasty.

459
00:36:24,307 --> 00:36:25,517
Why'd you come to my house today?

460
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:27,560
Mmm.

461
00:36:28,687 --> 00:36:30,271
Well, the factory was closed, so,

462
00:36:31,648 --> 00:36:33,982
I stopped by your home,
hoping you'd be around

463
00:36:33,983 --> 00:36:34,984
'cause I missed you.

464
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:40,114
You know the meth operation at…
Baekho Trading?

465
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:44,327
What are you talking about?

466
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:46,788
You drunk right now?

467
00:36:47,414 --> 00:36:49,124
Why did you close up shop there?

468
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:51,583
I bet your brother told you to.

469
00:36:51,584 --> 00:36:54,129
Slow down.
You do know who my brother is, right?

470
00:36:54,713 --> 00:36:57,297
- Director of the KCIA.
- Whoa.

471
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:59,591
You really think
you can threaten me, bitch?

472
00:36:59,592 --> 00:37:01,261
You're a two-bit prosecutor.

473
00:37:16,276 --> 00:37:19,695
You're turning into a junkie trying
to clean up after your brother, huh?

474
00:37:19,696 --> 00:37:21,530
- Let go!
- Baek Soyeong, listen.

475
00:37:21,531 --> 00:37:24,241
You know your brother's department
is weak now.

476
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:27,537
So get your head on straight
before you wind up in a world of hurt.

477
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:30,122
You know Choi Yuji, right?

478
00:37:30,123 --> 00:37:33,585
She's locked up at the Joint Investigation
Headquarters right now.

479
00:37:35,670 --> 00:37:38,214
You wanna stay out of prison
with your brother, right?

480
00:37:38,715 --> 00:37:40,215
Then I'd talk if I were you.

481
00:37:40,216 --> 00:37:41,884
Screw you.

482
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:43,261
Aren't you still a mother?

483
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:47,599
For your daughter's sake,
get off the junk already.

484
00:37:48,224 --> 00:37:50,268
Ugh, geez.

485
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:01,945
I hate that little shit.

486
00:38:01,946 --> 00:38:03,322
Hey, come here!

487
00:38:03,323 --> 00:38:05,157
Throw some salt outside!

488
00:38:05,158 --> 00:38:06,159
Damn it.

489
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:10,413
Oh.

490
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:16,211
Minju, there you are.

491
00:38:17,212 --> 00:38:18,755
Let's have a snack. Come here.

492
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:22,383
Hurry, let's go.

493
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:30,933
I was right.

494
00:38:30,934 --> 00:38:32,017
- Soyeong's an addict.
- Shit.

495
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:33,727
Start tracking down the other members.

496
00:38:33,728 --> 00:38:36,939
Yeah, but Jang told us
our priority should be the slush fund.

497
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:38,732
You sure this is okay?

498
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:40,735
Look, Baek's my target
for drug trafficking.

499
00:38:41,444 --> 00:38:43,530
He's the reason I wound up in Seoul.

500
00:38:44,239 --> 00:38:45,865
Right, let's go.

501
00:39:04,551 --> 00:39:05,969
Have you two met before today?

502
00:39:06,636 --> 00:39:08,762
Yes, we met one time, briefly.

503
00:39:08,763 --> 00:39:10,723
When the president was still alive.

504
00:39:13,017 --> 00:39:14,852
By the way, Director Baek,

505
00:39:14,853 --> 00:39:18,147
I can sense you're blessed
with remarkably good energy.

506
00:39:18,857 --> 00:39:20,024
Thank you, ma'am.

507
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:24,988
You two only met once
and she still recognizes you.

508
00:39:25,572 --> 00:39:26,781
I assume he…

509
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:29,450
he must've made quite an impression.

510
00:39:30,076 --> 00:39:31,953
Well, I suppose, I just

511
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:37,500
look at someone and say what I'm seeing.

512
00:39:39,168 --> 00:39:41,462
Madam Shin worked
for the president.

513
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:45,675
When he was in office,
she helped with a lot of major decisions.

514
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:50,763
She and I are quite close as well.

515
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:54,433
Oh. I see.

516
00:39:54,434 --> 00:39:55,768
Okay, so,

517
00:39:56,895 --> 00:40:00,022
the woman that's in prison,
you mentioned she's Japanese?

518
00:40:00,023 --> 00:40:01,024
Yes.

519
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:03,818
She's originally Zainichi Korean,

520
00:40:04,736 --> 00:40:06,737
but she managed
to get citizenship in Japan.

521
00:40:06,738 --> 00:40:10,158
Well, then, I should speak
to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

522
00:40:12,035 --> 00:40:15,705
If you end up getting involved personally,
it'll be a bad look for everyone.

523
00:40:17,790 --> 00:40:19,416
Well, since I've been having problems

524
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:21,669
thanks to the pricks
over at the JIH lately.

525
00:40:24,255 --> 00:40:26,799
I'm sure Director Baek can
handle the ledger on his own.

526
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:32,639
Would you work with me for a while
to help resolve some of these issues?

527
00:40:35,391 --> 00:40:36,892
What, for free?

528
00:40:39,228 --> 00:40:42,522
Come on, I'm not Hwang.
I don't expect any free favors.

529
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:46,193
You'll be well compensated
if things go off without a hitch.

530
00:40:51,240 --> 00:40:53,326
Don't worry, it was just a joke.

531
00:40:54,619 --> 00:40:56,245
You seem a little on edge today.

532
00:40:56,871 --> 00:40:59,665
Truth is, it really wouldn't
make a difference anyway.

533
00:40:59,666 --> 00:41:02,794
It's all in the name
of our country, isn't it?

534
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:07,173
In any case,

535
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:12,136
I'll pray nice and hard for both of you
from today onward, all right?

536
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:22,063
All right, turn your head a little.

537
00:41:22,730 --> 00:41:24,982
Mmm, a little further to the right.

538
00:41:27,527 --> 00:41:28,778
Thanks.

539
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,243
This is Baek Kihyun.

540
00:41:36,244 --> 00:41:37,536
You joined the JIH?

541
00:41:39,914 --> 00:41:40,998
Yes.

542
00:41:42,625 --> 00:41:44,419
How come you didn't say anything?

543
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:47,046
I was going to.

544
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:52,677
Jang Geonyoung's working there
as a special consultant, huh?

545
00:41:53,845 --> 00:41:54,846
Yes.

546
00:41:58,307 --> 00:42:00,308
Ahn put in a good word for him, I guess.

547
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:03,478
They're from the same town,
went to the same high school.

548
00:42:03,479 --> 00:42:06,149
These small town connections. Damn it.

549
00:42:08,526 --> 00:42:11,195
Don't get comfortable over there.

550
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:14,114
Jang Geonyoung specifically chose you

551
00:42:14,115 --> 00:42:17,285
because he wants to mess with your head.
You understand?

552
00:42:18,453 --> 00:42:19,579
Yeah. I'm aware.

553
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:21,706
About Colonel Baek…

554
00:42:23,416 --> 00:42:25,168
Shouldn't we get ahead of this?

555
00:42:26,127 --> 00:42:28,004
How long you plan to let him be?

556
00:42:28,838 --> 00:42:30,089
I could talk to him.

557
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:32,216
Just leave him alone.

558
00:42:33,051 --> 00:42:35,218
All these eyes on him, it won't be long.

559
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:37,889
He'll figure it out. He's not a child.

560
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:39,849
You think Baek would

561
00:42:40,391 --> 00:42:41,893
betray his own brother?

562
00:42:43,978 --> 00:42:46,272
Let's wait a bit longer
and see what he chooses.

563
00:42:47,148 --> 00:42:50,193
He either goes down with his brother,
or he survives with us.

564
00:42:51,652 --> 00:42:53,237
How's Choi Yuji holding up?

565
00:42:56,032 --> 00:42:59,035
Pretty good for now, I guess,
but it'll get worse.

566
00:42:59,619 --> 00:43:01,162
Believe me, she's solid.

567
00:43:02,038 --> 00:43:03,289
All you have to do

568
00:43:03,873 --> 00:43:06,209
is keep an eye on Jang
and report to me afterward.

569
00:43:07,627 --> 00:43:08,628
Yeah. I'm on it.

570
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:11,214
What about Soyeong?

571
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:13,633
Is she gonna be okay or what?

572
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:17,595
Don't worry about that.
She's not their target anyway.

573
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:19,722
Yes, sir. Copy that.

574
00:43:21,390 --> 00:43:22,600
Colonel Baek,

575
00:43:23,643 --> 00:43:24,893
you heading home yet?

576
00:43:24,894 --> 00:43:28,063
I've got a few things to do.
I'm just gonna finish up first.

577
00:43:28,064 --> 00:43:30,817
But it's getting late.
How about you finish in the morning?

578
00:43:31,317 --> 00:43:33,611
Soju sound good?
I'm buying the first round.

579
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:35,362
Sounds great.

580
00:43:35,363 --> 00:43:37,823
How about some dwaeji gukbap
and some makgeolli?

581
00:43:37,824 --> 00:43:39,991
You should head home, Colonel Ahn.

582
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:41,993
Your family's waiting.

583
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:43,037
I think

584
00:43:43,788 --> 00:43:45,164
it's just gonna be us.

585
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:49,334
- Okay, sure.
- All right.

586
00:43:49,335 --> 00:43:51,170
- I'll be waiting outside.
- Great.

587
00:44:08,396 --> 00:44:11,731
The memories are all rushing back to me,
sitting here with you.

588
00:44:11,732 --> 00:44:15,069
One night I was at this same table,
but I was with your brother.

589
00:44:15,611 --> 00:44:18,239
We had a bottle of soju, just like this.

590
00:44:19,532 --> 00:44:21,450
And we were here, eating dwaeji gukbap,

591
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:23,870
on a rainy night like tonight.

592
00:44:28,082 --> 00:44:29,625
What is it you want from me?

593
00:44:33,754 --> 00:44:35,173
Not much, to be honest.

594
00:44:35,882 --> 00:44:39,176
Well, actually, there is one thing.

595
00:44:39,177 --> 00:44:40,677
It's not a big deal.

596
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:42,013
Sorry, would you, um,

597
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:45,099
mind if I speak candidly
with you from now on?

598
00:44:45,725 --> 00:44:46,893
After all, we're a team now.

599
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:50,897
We are a team, aren't we?

600
00:44:52,148 --> 00:44:54,609
Oh, of course. Be candid.

601
00:44:55,359 --> 00:44:56,777
I knew it.

602
00:44:57,445 --> 00:45:00,405
You're just like your brother.
The boss man.

603
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:01,949
You're just as much
of a big shot as he is.

604
00:45:04,577 --> 00:45:06,579
Here you go. Let me pour you a drink.

605
00:45:07,622 --> 00:45:09,624
Look, stop beating around the bush.

606
00:45:10,541 --> 00:45:12,293
Why'd you bring me into the JIH?

607
00:45:26,933 --> 00:45:28,726
Use your head and look alive.

608
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:31,603
Okay, what exactly does that mean?

609
00:45:31,604 --> 00:45:33,814
You're better off taking it at face value.

610
00:45:34,315 --> 00:45:36,651
Just do your best to see things
as they are.

611
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:38,861
You're in a different world now.

612
00:45:40,947 --> 00:45:42,822
You can't keep living
like you always have.

613
00:45:46,619 --> 00:45:47,995
So I'm supposed to…

614
00:45:48,788 --> 00:45:50,498
to betray my own brother?

615
00:45:55,336 --> 00:45:56,337
Minju.

616
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,383
Who's gonna raise her?

617
00:46:01,217 --> 00:46:02,760
Are you willing to do that

618
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:05,346
if Baek Soyeong goes to jail?

619
00:46:17,191 --> 00:46:18,985
The truth is, uh…

620
00:46:22,571 --> 00:46:25,532
that your family complicates things
all the time, right?

621
00:46:25,533 --> 00:46:28,911
If you want your sister to live
and your niece to have a normal childhood,

622
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:33,165
you have to ensure you survive first.

623
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:37,169
What do you want?

624
00:46:38,296 --> 00:46:39,714
What do I have to do?

625
00:46:41,674 --> 00:46:44,885
Make sure you keep an eye
on Baek Kitae's activities.

626
00:46:45,511 --> 00:46:47,596
Watch him and find out what he's planning.

627
00:46:49,682 --> 00:46:51,851
You think your brother's gonna sit still?

628
00:46:52,727 --> 00:46:54,645
He's going to try something.

629
00:46:59,650 --> 00:47:01,444
You're in hell right now, aren't you?

630
00:47:03,112 --> 00:47:05,781
You want to escape that
and get your life back?

631
00:47:08,659 --> 00:47:09,660
Choice is yours.

632
00:47:11,370 --> 00:47:12,496
Pick a side.

633
00:47:16,584 --> 00:47:20,212
All right, then, how about we go elsewhere

634
00:47:21,297 --> 00:47:22,340
and get another round?

635
00:47:25,176 --> 00:47:26,927
This weather makes me thirsty.

636
00:47:27,762 --> 00:47:29,013
Mmm.

637
00:47:34,018 --> 00:47:35,227
Colonel Baek.

638
00:47:36,479 --> 00:47:37,772
See you tomorrow.

639
00:48:05,174 --> 00:48:08,093
♪ …toy train goes chugging along ♪

640
00:48:08,094 --> 00:48:11,429
♪ Carrying cookies and candy ♪

641
00:48:11,430 --> 00:48:14,183
Kitae, what on earth is going on?

642
00:48:16,811 --> 00:48:18,520
- The lab. Did you shut it down?
- Mm-hmm.

643
00:48:18,521 --> 00:48:20,980
I moved everything out after you called.

644
00:48:20,981 --> 00:48:23,066
All right, tell the others
to keep their mouths shut

645
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:24,443
and stay away from there for a while.

646
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:28,655
Wait, but don't tell me we're gonna
stop production for good. Are we?

647
00:48:28,656 --> 00:48:30,408
No, we won't be shutting down.
Why would we?

648
00:48:31,283 --> 00:48:33,326
We'll ramp back up
once things settle down.

649
00:48:33,327 --> 00:48:34,328
How long?

650
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:37,665
Just wait.

651
00:48:38,999 --> 00:48:40,917
First, I have to take back
what they stole.

652
00:48:40,918 --> 00:48:42,461
But what did they steal?

653
00:48:46,507 --> 00:48:49,844
♪ To our baby in Mom's room ♪

654
00:48:52,972 --> 00:48:55,015
Have a good day, Uncle Kitae.

655
00:48:55,599 --> 00:48:56,809
All right.

656
00:49:02,064 --> 00:49:05,191
♪ The little toy train
Goes chugging along-- ♪

657
00:49:05,192 --> 00:49:06,819
Go play somewhere else!

658
00:49:07,445 --> 00:49:08,863
Shit.

659
00:49:19,248 --> 00:49:20,708
Sir, I've got some news.

660
00:49:21,667 --> 00:49:22,710
What is it?

661
00:49:23,461 --> 00:49:25,671
A notice from
the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

662
00:49:28,674 --> 00:49:30,133
NOTICE REGARDING
DETAINED ZAINICHI KOREAN

663
00:49:30,134 --> 00:49:32,469
The Japanese government
has lodged a formal complaint.

664
00:49:32,470 --> 00:49:34,971
We also heard from
the Martial Law Command.

665
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:38,308
They both want Ikeda Yuji released,
effective immediately.

666
00:49:41,353 --> 00:49:44,147
- Yeah?
- Mr. Jang, this is the guard post.

667
00:49:44,148 --> 00:49:45,900
Your sister is here to see you, sir.

668
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:48,068
Put her on.

669
00:49:55,910 --> 00:49:58,453
Excuse me. Where's
the Joint Investigation Headquarters?

670
00:49:58,454 --> 00:50:00,622
Oh, the JIH? It's right over there.

671
00:50:00,623 --> 00:50:02,249
- Oh, thank you.
- Sure.

672
00:50:25,356 --> 00:50:28,067
- How can I help you?
- Uh…

673
00:50:31,654 --> 00:50:33,238
Hyeeun.

674
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:34,657
Oh, good morning.

675
00:50:35,324 --> 00:50:36,534
Come on in.

676
00:50:39,328 --> 00:50:41,746
I should introduce you to Colonel Baek.

677
00:50:41,747 --> 00:50:43,999
He and I have been working together.
Say hello.

678
00:50:44,917 --> 00:50:47,461
Right. Hello. Jang Hyeeun, sir.

679
00:50:48,712 --> 00:50:50,214
She's my sister.

680
00:50:52,633 --> 00:50:54,134
Baek Kihyun, Miss Jang.

681
00:50:56,679 --> 00:50:57,972
Let's go.

682
00:51:03,686 --> 00:51:06,564
I've heard so much
about this department lately.

683
00:51:07,231 --> 00:51:09,400
The JIH has been all over the news.

684
00:51:10,818 --> 00:51:12,194
So how have you been doing?

685
00:51:13,070 --> 00:51:14,905
You know, same as usual.

686
00:51:19,577 --> 00:51:21,912
What about you? Are you doing okay?

687
00:51:25,457 --> 00:51:27,001
Yeah, everything's fine.

688
00:51:28,377 --> 00:51:29,587
Why do you ask?

689
00:51:31,171 --> 00:51:32,756
You're thin and pale, Geonyoung.

690
00:51:34,216 --> 00:51:35,509
I'm getting worried about you.

691
00:51:36,552 --> 00:51:38,386
I've been busy, that's all.

692
00:51:38,387 --> 00:51:39,597
Don't worry, I'm okay.

693
00:51:42,516 --> 00:51:45,227
Hyeeun.

694
00:51:46,103 --> 00:51:48,022
I'm not the same man I used to be.

695
00:51:49,857 --> 00:51:50,899
You don't

696
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:53,819
need to worry about me, all right?

697
00:51:57,656 --> 00:52:00,074
But I still do. I can't help it.

698
00:52:15,799 --> 00:52:17,675
Hey, let me call you right back.

699
00:52:19,762 --> 00:52:22,514
Sorry. I'm being silly.

700
00:52:25,059 --> 00:52:26,393
I almost forgot.

701
00:52:27,728 --> 00:52:30,813
Here are some leftovers
from Dad's funeral yesterday.

702
00:52:30,814 --> 00:52:32,149
You should eat some of it.

703
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:39,031
I wish I'd been with you.

704
00:52:39,865 --> 00:52:41,116
I'm really sorry.

705
00:52:44,036 --> 00:52:45,620
It must've been hard on your own.

706
00:52:45,621 --> 00:52:47,538
Uh, not at all actually.

707
00:52:56,590 --> 00:52:57,591
Yes?

708
00:52:58,217 --> 00:52:59,677
Yeah, I'll be there soon.

709
00:53:00,761 --> 00:53:02,261
…will mostly be clear.

710
00:53:03,889 --> 00:53:06,349
…slightly lower
than yesterday, so it'll feel chilly.

711
00:53:06,350 --> 00:53:08,559
In Seoul, we're looking at a low
of 3 degrees Celsius…

712
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:12,773
Bring her here.

713
00:53:35,838 --> 00:53:37,380
Got her?

714
00:53:48,851 --> 00:53:50,436
Everyone out.

715
00:53:59,361 --> 00:54:00,862
Choi Yuji.

716
00:54:00,863 --> 00:54:02,740
Choi Yuji!

717
00:54:08,704 --> 00:54:12,875
We were contacted by the Japanese
Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

718
00:54:13,542 --> 00:54:15,043
It says right here…

719
00:54:17,296 --> 00:54:18,671
they want you released immediately.

720
00:54:32,352 --> 00:54:34,062
You think I'm gonna
let you walk out of here

721
00:54:35,022 --> 00:54:37,149
because of some official document? Huh?

722
00:54:46,617 --> 00:54:49,452
Tell me where the ledger is.

723
00:54:49,453 --> 00:54:52,997
Tell me where it is! Where is it? Come on!

724
00:54:52,998 --> 00:54:56,375
Answer me or you're dead.
Where's the ledger?

725
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:59,421
Say it! Where is it?

726
00:55:00,047 --> 00:55:03,133
Director Baek,
I found Takahashi Kazuo.

727
00:55:04,009 --> 00:55:05,134
Where is he?

728
00:55:05,135 --> 00:55:07,512
Busan Hotel. Room 308.

729
00:55:07,513 --> 00:55:09,264
Listen, stay until I get there.

730
00:55:09,806 --> 00:55:11,683
- I'm on the way now.
- Yes, sir.

731
00:56:13,203 --> 00:56:16,331
Where's the ledger?

732
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:27,467
What happened to the kumicho?

733
00:56:27,968 --> 00:56:29,970
We'll get her out soon, trust me on that.

734
00:56:30,721 --> 00:56:34,474
Until then, I'm gonna need you
to hand over the slush fund ledger.

735
00:56:35,434 --> 00:56:37,226
The kumicho said

736
00:56:37,227 --> 00:56:39,104
that I shouldn't give it to anyone.

737
00:56:40,856 --> 00:56:42,649
I already talked to Choi Yuji.

738
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:45,861
I won't be able to get her out
unless you hand it over.

739
00:56:46,987 --> 00:56:49,739
You know what happens
if that ledger gets picked up by the JIH?

740
00:56:49,740 --> 00:56:51,991
All of us are going down.

741
00:57:33,533 --> 00:57:34,826
Hang on.

742
00:57:37,162 --> 00:57:40,207
You mean you and the kumicho
had a conversation recently?

743
00:57:41,458 --> 00:57:45,087
The JIH took her into custody,
put her in some prison to torture her.

744
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:48,507
How could you have talked to her?

745
00:57:49,633 --> 00:57:52,928
Oh, you know,
you really ask too many questions.

746
00:58:25,460 --> 00:58:26,961
Bastard.

747
00:59:00,412 --> 00:59:02,163
Move!

748
00:59:07,043 --> 00:59:09,337
Oh, shit.

749
00:59:28,190 --> 00:59:29,399
Move!

750
01:00:29,709 --> 01:00:32,671
Well, Mr. Jang.

751
01:00:33,421 --> 01:00:35,006
You did a bang-up job here.

752
01:00:36,216 --> 01:00:38,175
Now that you've seen it,
what do you think?

753
01:00:42,180 --> 01:00:44,098
I think

754
01:00:44,099 --> 01:00:47,978
every single one of those pricks
is gonna wind up behind bars.

755
01:01:00,782 --> 01:01:02,242
That old geezer.

756
01:01:04,786 --> 01:01:06,413
He really held on, didn't he?

757
01:01:07,998 --> 01:01:10,792
Eighteen damn years in this chair.

758
01:01:13,587 --> 01:01:16,339
And just when I thought
it was finally my turn…

759
01:01:20,385 --> 01:01:21,678
Goddamn it.

760
01:01:23,555 --> 01:01:26,558
Looks like that bald asshole
Hwang is gonna take it.

761
01:01:29,311 --> 01:01:31,146
So, Kitae.

762
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:33,023
Yes, sir.

763
01:01:33,607 --> 01:01:35,483
What are you gonna do now?

764
01:01:38,028 --> 01:01:39,029
Huh?

765
01:01:41,072 --> 01:01:42,157
Hey.

766
01:01:45,076 --> 01:01:46,953
You just gonna go down like this?

767
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:54,960
There's something
I'd like your approval for.

768
01:01:54,961 --> 01:01:56,296
It's very important.

769
01:01:59,674 --> 01:02:00,717
Hwang Daesik.

770
01:02:01,968 --> 01:02:04,262
I wanna take care of him.
I'll do it myself.

771
01:02:06,806 --> 01:02:08,767
You really think you can handle that?

772
01:02:09,851 --> 01:02:11,394
Oh, it would be my pleasure.

773
01:02:11,978 --> 01:02:14,314
I'll do it my own way.
